{"schema": "rzl.doc.v1", "name": "NOTICE", "title": "Third-party notices: TinyEMU (MIT) · Linux 4.15 (GPL-2.0) · BusyBox 1.21.1 (GPL-2.0) · glibc 2.24.90 (LGPL-2.1) · bbl (BSD)", "rev": 2, "layer": "PUBLIC", "lang": "en", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "tag": "declared", "text": "Emulator: TinyEMU (RISC-V), compiled to WebAssembly as riscvemu64-wasm.{js,wasm}. Source: https://bellard.org/tinyemu/ · Demo pack: jslinux-2019-12-21.tar.gz · License: MIT (Fabrice Bellard, 2016-2017). SLIRP (if linked) is two-clause BSD; this egg ships with guest eth OFF (offline-first)."}, {"type": "text", "tag": "declared", "text": "Guest: Linux 4.15.0 riscv64 + BusyBox root filesystem from the same JSLinux demo pack (Buildroot-style). Kernel and rootfs are redistributed as part of that MIT-licensed demo. See LICENSE-TinyEMU.txt."}, {"type": "text", "tag": "declared", "text": "Why TinyEMU over v86: v86 (BSD-2-Clause, https://github.com/copy/v86) translates guest x86 to WASM at runtime (JIT). iOS WKWebView without a JIT entitlement is a poor fit. TinyEMU is ahead-of-time Emscripten WASM (interpreter-style), MIT, and includes VirtIO console/block/9P. Chosen for ЯSEED 0.1.5."}, {"type": "text", "tag": "observed", "text": "rev 2 (2026-10-11, append-only) CORRECTION of rev 1 block 2: the guest kernel and rootfs are NOT MIT. Only TinyEMU/JSLinux is MIT (LICENSE-TinyEMU.txt). Linux 4.15.0-00049-ga3b1e7a-dirty #11 is GPL-2.0 (licenses/COPYING.linux-4.15.txt). BusyBox v1.21.1 is GPL-2.0 (licenses/LICENSE.busybox-1.21.1.txt). glibc 2.24.90 in /lib is LGPL-2.1 (licenses/LGPL-2.1.glibc.txt). bbl (riscv-pk ac2c910) is BSD-3-Clause (licenses/LICENSE.riscv-pk-bbl.txt)."}, {"type": "text", "tag": "declared", "text": "Corresponding source: https://rizal.info/src/rvm-linux-0.1.0/ (mirror https://rizal.pw/src/rvm-linux-0.1.0/) — kernel.org linux-4.15 + the 49 riscv-linux commits to a3b1e7a + Bellard's riscv-linux.diff/config + BusyBox 1.21.1 source + licenses. Written offer (3 years) for the exact #11 kernel config, BusyBox .config and the glibc 2.24.90 snapshot: see SOURCE.rzl in this egg."}]}
